#12919
A Cavernous Room~
   You stand inside a massively-cavernous room whose expanse opens up before
you to the north. This place seems to defy logic, what would a room as big as
this be doing under here? The walls are smooth, polished stone which extend up
into darkness - you can barely make out the cathedral ceiling at the apex. In
the centre of the room, two massive stone pillars extend, supporting the
ceiling; their buttresses the only hint that they connect with it. You deduce
that you must, indeed, be far underground, because a room this high would be
impossible at any other altitude except for below sea level.
~
