#12942
A Dimly Lit Studio~
   Almost every surface of this dimly lit room is thickly splattered with
colorful oil paints, which nearly obscures the beautiful multi-colored dragons
that have been painted on the eastern wall. There are canvases littered
everywhere, some of them half-finished, others merely incomplete sketches.
It smells heavily of oil and pigment; apparently the artist whose studio this
is mixes his own paint. The only exit lies to the west, through the frail-
looking wooden door.
~
